        "The reading outlines an administrative proposal to extend the university library operating hours to twenty-four hours daily throughout the academic year. In the listening segment, the student enthusiastically supports the initiative, emphasizing that science and engineering students frequently work irregular hours on complex laboratory projects and require quiet study spaces outside conventional hours. The student notes that dormitories are often loud and unsuitable for late-night concentration, making a round-the-clock library an indispensable academic sanctuary for the student body."
